-- title:
--   Norm descent to the Gauss order and residue splitting
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ with a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$, modular polynomial data `data` for $q$ (a monic $\Phi\in\mathbb Z[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ killing $(j,j_q)$) together with the Kronecker congruence `hKr` identifying $\Phi \bmod q$ with $(Y^{q}-X)(Y-X^{q})$, integrality hypotheses $h\alpha,h\beta$ for the two Hecke embeddings `heckeAlphaBar`, `heckeBetaBar` at level $1$ and index $q$, and a place specialisation $P$ for these data. Let $R$ be a level-one prolongation pair for $P$, so in particular $R$ carries two regular prolongations $R_1,R_2$ of $A$ to $F:=\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(1\cdot q)$ with residue field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,1$, interchanged by the Fricke involution. Let $K_1$ be a field, an $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra mapping to $F$ compatibly, and assume Gauss transport for $R$ over $K_1$: an element of $K_1$ lands in $R_1.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when it lands in $R_2.\mathrm{integers}$. Put $V:=R.\mathrm{gaussBase}\,K_1$, the valuation subring of $K_1$ obtained by pulling back $R_1.\mathrm{integers}$, with residue field $\kappa$. Let $y,f\in F$ both lie in $R_1.\mathrm{integers}$ and in $R_2.\mathrm{integers}$ and be integral over $V$, and let $S:=V[y,f]$ be the Gauss order, the $V$-subalgebra of $F$ generated by $y$ and $f$. Assume: the elements `jFun` and `jqFun` (the images in $F$ of the $q$-expansions $j$ and $j(q\tau)$) lie in $S$; the $K_1$-span of $S$ is all of $F$; the two residue extensions $R.\mathrm{ResOne}$ and $R.\mathrm{ResTwo}$ (each a copy of the level-one modular function field over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$) have positive finite $\kappa$-dimension, and these dimensions add up to $[F:K_1]$; and each of the reduction maps $\rho_1,\rho_2\colon S\to R.\mathrm{ResOne},R.\mathrm{ResTwo}$ hits the element whose underlying Laurent series is $\mathrm{jqModC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)$. Then two things hold: $N_{F/K_1}(f)$ is the image in $K_1$ of the $V$-algebra norm of $f$ regarded as an element of $S$; and the residue in $\kappa$ of that norm equals the product of the $\kappa$-norms of $\rho_1(f)$ and $\rho_2(f)$.
--
--   This is the norm-docking step for a level-one prolongation pair: it identifies the field norm of $f$ with its norm computed in the Gauss order $V[y,f]$, and factors the reduction of that norm across the two residue components of the pair. It is used by the summed Gauss-pencil laws [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.LevelOneProlongationPair.sum_filter_value_eq_ord_add_sum_roots`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.LevelOneProlongationPair.sum_filter_value_eq_ord_add_sum_roots) and [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.LevelOneProlongationPair.sum_filter_value_eq_sum_roots_add`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.LevelOneProlongationPair.sum_filter_value_eq_sum_roots_add).
